The WHATWG character-encoding label table in `Sources/RivuletCore/Reader/Charset/` is transcribed
 from `golang.org/x/text` (encoding/htmlindex), which is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License;
 the table itself is published by the WHATWG Encoding Standard. The UTF-8 error rule and the
 encoding-detection order follow `golang.org/x/text` (encoding/unicode) and
 `golang.org/x/net/html/charset`, also BSD 3-Clause. The named character reference table in
 `Sources/RivuletCore/Reader/XML/` is transcribed from the Go standard library (`encoding/xml`,
 `HTMLEntity`), also BSD 3-Clause. The named character reference table in
 `Sources/RivuletCore/Reader/Sanitizer/HTMLEntityTable.swift` is generated from
 `golang.org/x/net/html` (`entity` and `entity2`), and the HTML tokenizer subset and the insertion
 modes the sanitizer reads through follow the same package, also BSD 3-Clause. The layout engine,
 chunk scanner and reading primitives in `Sources/RivuletCore/Reader/Date/` follow the Go standard
 library (`time`, `time/format.go`), also BSD 3-Clause. https://cs.opensource.google/go/x/text
